  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (3000) and comparing how often each lottery exceeds this level. Lottery A exceeds it 45% of the time; Lottery B never exceeds it. The reason would thus favor A. However, the individual expresses a preference for a 'safe, smaller amount,' which aligns more with preferring Lottery B due to its high probability (90%) of a non-zero outcome. This suggests the individual is focusing on security and avoiding zero, not on exceeding an aspiration level of 3000. The individual does not reference any calculation of an average outcome or evaluate outcomes relative to 3000. The justification is consistent with a risk-averse or certainty-seeking heuristic, not the aspiration-level rule described. Therefore, there is no evidence that the individual used the aspiration-level reason; in fact, the reasoning appears to conflict with it.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
