{
  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on an aspiration level defined as the mean of all outcomes in the decision problem, ignoring their probabilities. The outcomes in the problem are 1000, 0 (from Lottery A) and 500 (from Lottery B). The mean of these outcomes is (1000 + 0 + 500) / 3 = 500. The aspiration level is therefore 500. The reason evaluates each lottery based on the probability of yielding an outcome above this aspiration level (i.e., >500). For Lottery A: 1000 > 500 occurs with 50% probability, 0 > 500 does not occur, so the probability of a positive difference is 50%. For Lottery B: 500 > 500 is false (since it's equal), so the probability of a positive difference is 0%. Thus, the decision reason would prefer Lottery A over Lottery B because it has a higher probability (50% vs 0%) of exceeding the aspiration level.",
