  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level (500) as the mean of all outcomes and comparing each lottery based on the probability of exceeding this value. The individual does mention 500€ and 1000€, and the aspiration level (500) coincides with the outcome of B. However, the individual does not compute or reference any such mean, nor do they evaluate how often each lottery exceeds 500. Instead, they treat the 500€ as a secure base for future gain, not as a threshold for evaluating gains vs. losses. The justification is forward-looking and pragmatic (investment potential), not based on frequency of exceeding an aspiration level. There is no indication that the individual computed differences between outcomes and an aspiration level or considered probabilities of positive deviations. The reasoning is more aligned with security-seeking or future opportunity valuation than with the aspiration-level rule as defined.",
